  "recommendations": [
    "Moonshine FP32 eager is the best short-job profile on this RTX 4090. Use FP16 only for memory pressure; it reduced peak allocation by 40.30% but was 5.00% slower on this sample.",
    "Moonshine torch.compile is useful only for a long-lived high-volume process: steady mean latency improved 41.52%, but setup took about 76 seconds and broke even after about 608 same-length utterances.",
    "Whisper-tiny FP32 was faster than FP16 and BF16. Reduced precision saved 16.25% peak allocation but increased mean latency by 15-16%.",
    "Wav2Vec2 BF16 had the best mean and cut peak allocation by 44.46%, but the host timings were highly bimodal; treat the 1.14x mean speedup as checkpoint- and machine-specific.",
    "For CPU Silero and the Sherpa-compatible Silero wrapper, one intra-op thread was substantially faster than 48 threads with identical segment boundaries.",
    "Silero torch.compile improved steady one-thread latency by 14.76% but increased process peak RSS by 64.52%; eager one-thread is the default recommendation.",
    "No precision or compile profile is claimed quality-neutral beyond this single checkpoint-specific sample. Validate WER/CER on the target dataset before deployment."
  ]
}
